# /sdlc-implement $ARGUMENTS

The person asked you to implement the feature `$ARGUMENTS` from its specification. **You are the agent; `./scripts/sdlc` is the judge.**
`./scripts/sdlc implement` normally does the steps below around an agent it starts itself. In this chat you are already that agent, so you do those
steps yourself, in this order, and the tool's own checks decide whether the work is done. Never say "done" for anything you did not see pass.

On Windows PowerShell or cmd, write `.\scripts\sdlc.cmd` wherever this says `./scripts/sdlc`.

## 0. Which feature

- No feature given: list the folders in `.ai/specs/` (not `_template`, not `FEAT-000`), say that you need one, and stop.
  If they have none of their own yet, point to `/sdlc-new <slug>` (write a spec in chat) or `/sdlc-spec <document>` (draft one from a requirements document).
- `FEAT-000` is the worked example. Its code and tests already ship with this project, so there is nothing to implement. Say so, suggest
  `/sdlc-verify` to see it proven and `/sdlc-new <slug>` to start a feature of their own, and stop.

## 1. Start from the state the tool requires

1. `git status --short`: only the feature's own spec folder may be uncommitted (`.ai/evidence/` is ignored). Anything else: list it, ask the person to
   commit or stash it so they can review exactly what you change, and stop.
2. Fingerprint the spec so you can prove you did not touch it. For an id like `FEAT-001` its folder is `.ai/specs/FEAT-001-*/`:
   `git hash-object .ai/specs/$ARGUMENTS-*/prd.md .ai/specs/$ARGUMENTS-*/acceptance.json`. Keep the two hashes.
3. `./scripts/sdlc sync` installs the toolchain if it is missing (it does nothing when everything is current).
4. `./scripts/sdlc gates` must be green **before** you change anything, so every later failure is yours. Red? Show the person which gate and stop.

## 2. Get the exact prompt the CLI would send an agent

`./scripts/sdlc implement $ARGUMENTS --dry-run --agent claude` runs nothing and starts no agent. It checks that the spec is complete (if not, it says what is
missing: tell the person, and stop) and prints `prompt: .ai/evidence/<run>/implement.prompt.md`.

**Read that whole file and do what it says.** It holds the PRD, every check, this repository's rules and playbooks, which files are protected, and the
hard rules. One thing changes because you can talk to the person: where it says to write questions to a file and stop, ask the person here and wait
for the answer instead of guessing.

## 3. Build it

Follow the prompt: tests first (watch each fail for the right reason), then the simplest code that passes, one acceptance criterion at a time.
After adding a dependency to a manifest run `./scripts/sdlc sync`. Iterate quickly with `./scripts/sdlc gates --only <gate-id>`.
Do not edit the specification or any protected file, and never weaken, skip or delete a test or a threshold to get green.

## 4. Check you stayed inside the rules

- `git hash-object` on the same two spec files must print the same two hashes as in step 1.
- `git status --short -- .ai/sdlc.json scripts .github/workflows` must print nothing (also nothing for any other path under `integrity.protected` in `.ai/sdlc.json`).
- `git log --oneline -3` must show no commit made by you. Never commit, push, reset or stash: the person reviews `git diff` and commits.

If any of these fails, undo your change to that file (`git checkout -- <path>`), say what happened, and continue.

## 5. Prove it, and heal

`./scripts/sdlc verify` runs every gate and then checks each acceptance criterion against the **running** system. That starts the whole stack and can take
minutes: give the command up to 10 minutes (or run it in the background and wait for it).

- Green (exit 0): go to step 6.
- Red: read `.ai/evidence/latest/report.md` and the log it points to, fix the **code** (not the spec, not the checks), run `./scripts/sdlc verify` again.
- It cannot start the system at all (for example Docker is not running): that is not yours to fix and it does not count as a round. Say what it printed, tell the
  person to start Docker (or to change `runtime.mode` in `.ai/sdlc.json`, which only they may edit), and stop.
- Stop and report instead of looping on when `verify` has failed <%maxIterations%> times, or when the same checks fail with the same errors <%noProgressLimit%> times in a row.
  Say what fails, what you tried, and what you think is wrong. The person decides.

## 6. Report

Finish with: for each acceptance criterion, the test(s) and the check id(s) that prove it; anything you could not verify and why; and the reminder that
**nothing is committed**: review with `git diff`, then commit and open a PR. The evidence is in `.ai/evidence/latest/report.md`.

## Never

- Run `./scripts/sdlc implement` without `--dry-run`, or `spec`, `feature`, `loop` or `deploy`: they start another agent, wait for a person, or change a real environment.
- Commit, push, change git configuration, or put secrets anywhere.
- Claim a pass you did not see in this chat.
